 group that happens to have a supernatural patron; outside of that totem (who, by the way, is cartoonishly powerful at Rank 10) they have nothing to do with the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-15-2017, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T10:34:15-07:00","id":1092858,"title":"","content":"they really sound more like a cult than a conspiracy- some cults may be conspiracies, but it's not the other way around. The main defining feature of conspiracies is that they hunt- they uphold the Vigil, searching for monsters or supernatural phenomena and work against it, one way or another (most of them try to kill them, sure, but more than one Compact has other objectives in mind). Protecting Mother Earth could be their reason to exist, but they need something more- like, why do they hunt monsters in order to protect her. The Keepers of the Source may answer that niche, one way or another, but some people don't seem to like them, and I think it is better than open this can of worms in here :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T02:33:45-07:00","id":1093164,"title":"","content":"then i might make them a cult but 1st how to salvge it as a conspiracy <br /> 1st well vampires tend to be big corps owners so maybe they fight vampires <br /> 2ed well cult time ok how would you do this i think i told that every dot of Shadow Cult Initiation has a benefit so i have som ideas but what about you guys your the pro at homebrew","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T18:41:37-07:00","id":1093487,"title":"","content":"Is this Conspiracy supposed to be the Planeteers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:09:32-07:00","id":1093491,"title":"","content":"Nah just similar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T02:16:25-07:00","id":1094465,"title":"","content":"1 dot gives you a 1 dot or 2 dot Mentor Mentor<br /> 2 dot gives you a specialty depending on what faction the user is on<br /> 3 dot gives you a plus 4 to breaking points related to helping the environment like killing the owner of a cool factory<br /> 4 dot gets you a 4 dot retraner<br /> 5 dot gets you a use of the endowment i mentioned with a roll to make the rank 10 spirit mother earth do anything related to helping the environment but not anything the spirit dos not care about and only once per chronicle<br /> so it can get rid of your cancer bot not all cancer because the rank 10 spirit of cancer would fight mother earth and she dos not want that and not give the user the meaning of life because she dos not know that and anything shellfish like that would kill the user with no roll<br /> well any thoughts please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T07:32:07-07:00","id":1094861,"title":"","content":"Rank 10 spirit? Contact with such a being simply isn't possible, for the same reason humans can't make intelligent contact with fleas and gnats. You're talking about The spirit of the universe here. We already have Gaea, spirit of the planet Earth whose body is sometimes suspected to be the <i>entire Spirit World itself </i>and who may not even properly exist as an individual being because she's just that vast, as Rank 9. Even the Uratha aren't sure about whether Gaea really exists, because a being of that high Rank is incomprehensible even to the half-natives of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> If you just want a powerful spiritual patron who gives the hunter-cultists a mission every now and then, and sometimes intervene on their behalf to perform miracles for them, you can just... do so without bothering to developing the details of that patron. In fact, Rank 6+ spirits, who are the most likely candidates for your purpose, don't even have stat blocks because the Ephemeral Entities rules can't properly represent them. When they need something done, they just do it. If they have limits to their actions, it isn't something a mere human can comprehend and thus is irrelevant for the hunters.<br /> <br /> Assuming you still want these guys as a hunter Conspiracy and not a Mystery Cult, I suggest keeping the environmentalist themes in and refer to Werewolf The Apocalypse. The protagonists of that gameline, the Garou, are still very much fanatical and cult-like in their behavior, but the heroic actions they pull off every now and then and the enemies they fight should give you ideas on how to shape out your own homebrew. And even if you do want this group as a Mystery Cult, WtA can still help because, well, environmentalist bio-weapons running on spiritual rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T08:34:24-07:00","id":1094871,"title":"","content":"Now i will have to do more research thanks though but maybe this wasn't meant to work out<br /> so next groups involve gangsters who are able to make changling plages and whose purpose is to support the don","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T08:35:32-07:00","id":1094872,"title":"","content":"Mostly because i Don't think i can pay for wta","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T08:46:45-07:00","id":1094874,"title":"","content":"Surfing through sites such as White Wolf Wikia and the relevant forums can help, though.<br /> <br /> As for the gangsters, since they're still hunters who go up against monsters in the dark, they'll get into vigilante territory. A canon hunter Compact, the Night Watch, are composed of such street-level vigilantes, whose primary enemies are vampires that prey on the people living in their neighborhoods. Just make sure that gangsters are still gangsters, that they're still criminals who leach off society, and the concept is solid. Since you're giving them fae pledges, maybe their primary enemies are changelings who cause mayhem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:21:27-07:00","id":1094928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1092769-conspiracy-ideas?p=1094874#post1094874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the gangsters, since they're still hunters who go up against monsters in the dark, they'll get into vigilante territory. A canon hunter Compact, the Night Watch, are composed of such street-level vigilantes, whose primary enemies are vampires that prey on the people living in their neighborhoods. Just make sure that gangsters are still gangsters, that they're still criminals who leach off society, and the concept is solid. Since you're giving them fae pledges, maybe their primary enemies are changelings who cause mayhem?</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to that, look up the spoilers/concepts for Goblin Contracts, and Goblin Debt. Maybe the Hunters have access to a special Goblin Contract that lets them form Pledges of their own. Maybe they even got it by acting as some kind of Goblin Debt Collectors on Ironside/the real world? Conflict with Changelings, then, is baked right in - the Hunters are acting as supernatural repo-men, in addition to eliminating competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T19:09:01-07:00","id":1094987,"title":"","content":"Well that can work i will then need to make the don a goblin and by the way the dons the whole purpose of the conspiracy so the hunters take care of humens and supernatural especially changlings due to there love of deals making it easyer to work with g them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T23:26:32-07:00","id":1097436,"title":"","content":