a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 things<br /> 1 the weapon of last resort dos not get downgraded to bashing and ageis telasmen dos not need willpower for the armer just for the fear effect</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, Vampires didn't downgrade much damage anyways, so I'm not sure that is really significant. And, okay, the Aegis Talisman used willpower for the Fear effect, but other than that it was still just armor that required 5 dots in the Endowment to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1092769-conspiracy-ideas?p=1102993#post1102993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 well It's ment to be like a werewolf in war ftom so thats why plus at low levels it bearly dos anything and if more then one person attacks you in 1 trun then your screwed plue mosters can some times avg damage then your still screwed and if mind controled well you get the idea its not ment to make you unkillable its ment to give some searvablety to characters that might need it stroy wise maybe with bio engineering they get rid of the silver weekness and most likely im giving silver weekness</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves in Garau form are exceptional, and have the whole Death Rage thing. As for more than one person attacking - yeah, so? That's a problem with healing no matter what. Numbers will do you in. Aggravated damage is supposed to be a special case, and not what is normally planed around (based on how difficult it is to inflict in most cases). As for engineering out the silver weakness - how? It isn't some genetic quirk - it is a spiritual curse. If you are borrowing Werewolf regen, you get the curse, unless you've somehow made a better deal with Luna than Werewolves have had (<i>maybe</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1092769-conspiracy-ideas?p=1102993#post1102993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 thats how revivfy works no change other then getting rid os stamina cost so people dont just pick supel instead plus like the dread power if you read it it says if killed by avg damage then your screwed plus we are adding the week of vulnerability plus dice are random so yeah</div> </div> </div> </div>Revivify costs Stamina per attempt, and rolls dice because the outcome has impact (regarding perma death, lost Stamina, revive, or revive even with Aggravated Damage). Since you are creating a power that <i>isn't</i> Revivify, why are it's limitation assumed? The Stamina cost is a significant limiter to repeated use in Revivify. As far as I knew, you just had an easy roll to resurrect, no cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1092769-conspiracy-ideas?p=1102993#post1102993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class